            {
                "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                "word": "relativity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a2bb5080-90c7-4207-85a9-03002c5b15f6",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "relativities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdc9e88f-d059-3a1d-86b3-0f3cf5024137",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being relative to something else; the absence of universally applicable rules or standards; relativism; (countable) an instance of this."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "83357d8a-f888-3fc9-b143-0857ffddeb3f",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of principle of relativity (“the principle that the laws of physics should be the same for all observers”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "ellipsis",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ca879d7d-f6bf-3213-8c0a-14a60f7a5c89",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of principle of relativity (“the principle that the laws of physics should be the same for all observers”).",
                            "Also Einsteinian relativity: the reliance of the nature of physical phenomena (such as gravity, light, mass, and time) on the relative motion between an observer and the thing observed, as developed by Albert Einstein in two theories, special relativity and general relativity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "specifically",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1937a4ad-b2ed-3270-8972-74e2cdacdd74",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An evaluation of the similarities and differences between things; a comparison; hence, a difference in position or status between things; a disparity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "in-plural",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d1ccd20-fe52-354c-8436-5c7599282cec",
                        "entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An evaluation of the similarities and differences between things; a comparison; hence, a difference in position or status between things; a disparity.",
                            "The difference in pay or positions between different employees in a business (internal relativity), or between different businesses (external relativity); a differential."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "in-plural",
                            "specifically",
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f273f5c-3ac8-4347-8799-91ee412a05a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state of being relative to something else — see also relativism",
                        "target_lang_word": "relativnost",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3c2792b-690a-4de7-b229-c6c7186847b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state of being relative to something else — see also relativism",
                        "target_lang_word": "relativita",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "703f6311-a6b3-410b-bfdb-e20ccfeade8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state of being relative to something else — see also relativism",
                        "target_lang_word": "relativité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "relativité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e751e59-fcf6-371f-83e3-7daadbe25013",
                                        "entry_id": "2c92d6a1-4a73-30da-a910-282e9e2ae096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ce qui est relatif, ce qui dépend d’autre chose qui n’est pas une vérité intangible en soi, qui n’est ni autonome ni intrinsèque."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87717a01-899a-4cda-9d9a-d10d4af14405",
                                                "sense_id": "2e751e59-fcf6-371f-83e3-7daadbe25013",
                                                "text": "Croyez bien que la relativité de la durée passionne moins les métaphysiciens que les amants…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ea74105-32ea-4e6b-8d4c-83c915e5636e",
                                                "sense_id": "2e751e59-fcf6-371f-83e3-7daadbe25013",
                                                "text": "Il sait aussi la relativité de son savoir. Tôt ou tard, comme il l'a fait lui aussi, on reprendra le sujet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fb1db47-95fc-32e6-b561-a86bc41de953",
                                        "entry_id": "2c92d6a1-4a73-30da-a910-282e9e2ae096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère de ce qui est opposé mais indissociable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d3fa66-241f-412e-9dc6-1dec9a79c861",
                                                "sense_id": "6fb1db47-95fc-32e6-b561-a86bc41de953",
                                                "text": "La relativité exprime l’interdépendance de deux termes opposés qui ne peuvent être définis l’un sans l’autre (comme, par exemple, le double et la moitié, le grand et le petit. (Aristote)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1f26512-6ab7-3332-ac64-3e64333ce35b",
                                        "entry_id": "2c92d6a1-4a73-30da-a910-282e9e2ae096",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Théorie générale de la physique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e2e0854-aa30-4bd4-8408-725cdd7ece25",
                                                "sense_id": "c1f26512-6ab7-3332-ac64-3e64333ce35b",
                                                "text": "Peu après, M. J.-P. Vigier a signalé une analogie profonde entre mes idées sur les ondes à singularités et les tentatives de M. Einstein pour représenter les particules matérielles comme des singularités du champ dans le cadre de la Relativité généralisée."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "081703f8-a3ec-44f9-b02c-c66a2d24145f",
                                                "sense_id": "c1f26512-6ab7-3332-ac64-3e64333ce35b",
                                                "text": "Remarquons d’entrée de jeu qu’il faut méconnaître le père de la théorie de la relativité pour imaginer qu’il ait pu assimiler l’astrologie à une « science »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4955299a-e14d-4e83-9442-5311d35078c4",
                                                "sense_id": "c1f26512-6ab7-3332-ac64-3e64333ce35b",
                                                "text": "Ce chef de gouvernement capable de discuter avec Einstein la théorie de la relativité de l’espace et du temps emprunte à sa vie intérieure un incomparable prestige."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f94434de-a29a-4292-88bb-20f440d556ac",
                        "source_entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state of being relative to something else — see also relativism",
                        "target_lang_word": "Relativität",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Relativität",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4072517e-48e0-3679-861f-4a3764cd8b60",
                                        "entry_id": "3234b890-fe14-318f-ba38-00cbdaeb59b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Eigenschaft einer Erscheinung/eines Phänomens, von anderen Gegebenheiten abhängig zu sein"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ee03a40-2c56-467b-8f8d-7f2c2ec9b002",
                                                "sense_id": "4072517e-48e0-3679-861f-4a3764cd8b60",
                                                "text": "„Damit wird eine unhintergehbare Relativität der Standpunkte und Perspektiven geschaffen - eine Relativität im Wortsinne, denn das Individuum steht immer in Relation zu anderen, wobei diese Differenz durch die Relativität der Perspektive gerade nicht überbrückt wird.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55d0e279-b12f-42a1-a2a0-73b06f94c955",
                                                "sense_id": "4072517e-48e0-3679-861f-4a3764cd8b60",
                                                "text": "„Das schließt aber keineswegs Relativitäten aus. So ist – a priori – die Gesamtsphäre der körperlichen Natur eine Sphäre von Relativitäten. Körperliches Sein ist Sein in einem Zusammenhang endloser Relativitäten.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ddc1a7f-5087-3946-bae2-0c40f0f29d7d",
                                        "entry_id": "3234b890-fe14-318f-ba38-00cbdaeb59b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Eigenschaft einer Erscheinung/eines Phänomens, nur unter gewissen Umständen Gültigkeit zu haben"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cc4ce48-443f-4385-9ad5-ae3665b73733",
                                                "sense_id": "4ddc1a7f-5087-3946-bae2-0c40f0f29d7d",
                                                "text": "„Neben dieser offenen und fragmentarischen Gestalt ist aber eine Relativität auch des Geltungsanspruchs dieses Wissenschaftssystems festzustellen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc0ef06a-780b-4e3f-93e1-999b6fcc7937",
                        "source_entry_id": "27df8ac8-9172-3f0c-87f3-ec94843ee2b2",
